                            <comment id="15661509" author="bzz" created="Sun, 13 Nov 2016 13:45:46 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agoodman&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agoodman&quot;&gt;agoodman&lt;/a&gt; if you have some time, could you please take a look?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15661813" author="agoodman" created="Sun, 13 Nov 2016 17:28:13 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=bzz&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;bzz&quot;&gt;bzz&lt;/a&gt; Can&apos;t believe I missed this. The &lt;tt&gt;Py4jZeppelinContext&lt;/tt&gt; constructor needs an additional line which calls the superclass constructor in-order to set the &lt;tt&gt;_displayhook&lt;/tt&gt; attribute. This is a very easy fix.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
