                            <comment id="15662304" author="agoodman" created="Sun, 13 Nov 2016 23:25:02 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I recall having a problem similar to this one in the past, since I know that the current python interpreter impl is very picky about whitespace and indentation (to an incorrect degree, as we both know). What&apos;s strange in this case is that you are having this problem but I am not. Maybe you should try adding some extra logging in &lt;tt&gt;PythonInterpreter.java&lt;/tt&gt; which prints out the exact text being loaded &lt;tt&gt;bootstrap.py&lt;/tt&gt; into the interpreter on your end.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15662313" author="agoodman" created="Sun, 13 Nov 2016 23:31:31 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=bzz&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;bzz&quot;&gt;bzz&lt;/a&gt; I think I have found the source of the problem. I&apos;ll submit a PR shortly for you to test, though it will be under &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-1656&quot; title=&quot;z.show in Python interpreter does not work&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-1656&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;ZEPPELIN-1656&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15662321" author="bzz" created="Sun, 13 Nov 2016 23:36:16 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Thank you! I did enabled DEBUG logging, and here is something else found in the logs, which was never shown in GUI:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;  File &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;&amp;lt;stdin&amp;gt;&quot;&lt;/span&gt;, line 1, in &amp;lt;module&amp;gt;
